      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even we avoid most i2c write, we only decrease almost half of the option 0 register i2c operations. Still a lot more than patch 2 does. Also, if i2c read return garbage value, it can give wrong inhibit bit value. This will cause us write back with garbage value.\nsince charger_set_option() is the only place to write to option 0, it\u0027s sure prev_mode stores the genuine value of inhibit bit. This can minimize read/write operation. It\u0027s safer. We did test with this also. If possible, I will suggest we go with patch 2.",
